[{:db/id 17592186064306 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-09ef39a3-aa47-5850-a2b1-1c368b15a626"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-09ef39a3-aa47-5850-a2b1-1c368b15a626" :question/id #uuid "09ef39a3-aa47-5850-a2b1-1c368b15a626" :question/math-academy-id "q-2523" :question/problem "Consider the function $y={x}^{(2x+1)}.$ Its derivative is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={x}^{2x}\\cdot g(x).\n$$\n\nFind the function $g(x).$" :question/worked-solution "We have the function \n\n$$\ny={x}^{2x+1}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we take the natural logarithm of both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2x+1}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =(2x+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((2x+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x+1)\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+(2x+1)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡x+(2x+1)\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\frac{2x+1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y(\\frac{2x+1}{x}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $y={x}^{2x+1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={x}^{2x+1}(\\frac{2x+1}{x}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x) \\\\  & ={x}^{2x+1}(\\frac{2x+1}{x}+\\frac{2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}) \\\\  & ={x}^{2x}\\cdot x(\\frac{2x+1}{x}+\\frac{2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}) \\\\  & ={x}^{2x}(2x+2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x)=2x+2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4522aec1-18fc-5a98-a19b-f2258fae7499"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4522aec1-18fc-5a98-a19b-f2258fae7499" :answer-field/id #uuid "4522aec1-18fc-5a98-a19b-f2258fae7499" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e7caf4ba-0364-56de-9d87-fa137b1cb670" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e7caf4ba-0364-56de-9d87-fa137b1cb670" "answer-cd4c6e33-c46b-5d45-876e-4d7c5861b00b" "answer-438050ca-5554-5efb-b6ab-495501b5ed22" "answer-05f33a63-c291-5841-be1b-4faff432cabd" "answer-fd40483e-6c18-50b5-b937-12944951fb45"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e7caf4ba-0364-56de-9d87-fa137b1cb670" :answer/id #uuid "e7caf4ba-0364-56de-9d87-fa137b1cb670" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x+2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cd4c6e33-c46b-5d45-876e-4d7c5861b00b" :answer/id #uuid "cd4c6e33-c46b-5d45-876e-4d7c5861b00b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-438050ca-5554-5efb-b6ab-495501b5ed22" :answer/id #uuid "438050ca-5554-5efb-b6ab-495501b5ed22" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-05f33a63-c291-5841-be1b-4faff432cabd" :answer/id #uuid "05f33a63-c291-5841-be1b-4faff432cabd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fd40483e-6c18-50b5-b937-12944951fb45" :answer/id #uuid "fd40483e-6c18-50b5-b937-12944951fb45" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064307 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-bc4aa46c-af83-51d5-a531-dab6715c6436"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-bc4aa46c-af83-51d5-a531-dab6715c6436" :question/id #uuid "bc4aa46c-af83-51d5-a531-dab6715c6436" :question/math-academy-id "q-138807" :question/problem "Consider the function $y=(3{x}^{2})^{x}.$ Its derivative is given by \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=(3{x}^{2})^{x}\\cdot g(x).\n$$\n\nFind the function $g(x).$" :question/worked-solution "We have the function \n\n$$\ny=(3{x}^{2})^{x}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we take the natural logarithm of both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡((3{x}^{2})^{x}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3{x}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3{x}^{2})) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot {y}^{′} & =(x)^{′}\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3{x}^{2}))+(x)\\cdot {(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3{x}^{2}))}^{′} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot {y}^{′} & =1\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡(3{x}^{2})+x\\cdot (\\frac{1}{3{x}^{2}}\\cdot 6x) \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{′}}{y} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3{x}^{2})+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for ${y}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =y(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3{x}^{2})+2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $y=(3{x}^{2})^{x}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =(3{x}^{2})^{x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3{x}^{2})+2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3{x}^{2})+2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1814a4c4-4f4b-5074-b701-a59013925f9c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1814a4c4-4f4b-5074-b701-a59013925f9c" :answer-field/id #uuid "1814a4c4-4f4b-5074-b701-a59013925f9c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-090603b9-f435-5f7d-81b3-5fa7d70d5ed1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-090603b9-f435-5f7d-81b3-5fa7d70d5ed1" "answer-bfdefb81-a578-5bb1-b28c-f155bdc49d7b" "answer-57d95622-82b3-5393-b370-8d92f43e6f97" "answer-60eefb25-daf9-5e08-b4ef-37256dd0bc7a" "answer-4902eb83-e8de-509d-9be7-218c3d06e15f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-090603b9-f435-5f7d-81b3-5fa7d70d5ed1" :answer/id #uuid "090603b9-f435-5f7d-81b3-5fa7d70d5ed1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3{x}^{2})+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bfdefb81-a578-5bb1-b28c-f155bdc49d7b" :answer/id #uuid "bfdefb81-a578-5bb1-b28c-f155bdc49d7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3{x}^{2})+2x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-57d95622-82b3-5393-b370-8d92f43e6f97" :answer/id #uuid "57d95622-82b3-5393-b370-8d92f43e6f97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3{x}^{2})+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-60eefb25-daf9-5e08-b4ef-37256dd0bc7a" :answer/id #uuid "60eefb25-daf9-5e08-b4ef-37256dd0bc7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3{x}^{2})+x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4902eb83-e8de-509d-9be7-218c3d06e15f" :answer/id #uuid "4902eb83-e8de-509d-9be7-218c3d06e15f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186064308 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-82f90d91-406e-5d3c-bce9-9c8235648ab0"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-82f90d91-406e-5d3c-bce9-9c8235648ab0" :question/id #uuid "82f90d91-406e-5d3c-bce9-9c8235648ab0" :question/math-academy-id "q-138851" :question/problem "Consider the function $y=(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)^{2x}.$ Its derivative is given by \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)^{2x}\\cdot g(x).\n$$\n\nFind the function $g(x).$" :question/worked-solution "We have the function \n\n$$\ny=(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)^{2x}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we take the natural logarithm of both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡((\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)^{2x}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡y & =2x\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)) \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot {y}^{′} & =(2x)^{′}\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x))+(2x)\\cdot {(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x))}^{′} \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\cdot {y}^{′} & =2\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)+2x\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}\\cdot {sec}^{2}⁡x) \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{′}}{y} & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)+2x\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{′}}{y} & =2(\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)+x\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\,)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve for ${y}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =2y(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)+x\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we substitute $y=(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)^{2x}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =2(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)^{2x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)+x\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)+x\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡x.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6da65985-bad5-5a30-9563-e72ed071e141"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6da65985-bad5-5a30-9563-e72ed071e141" :answer-field/id #uuid "6da65985-bad5-5a30-9563-e72ed071e141" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ead5149a-8ad0-50cd-aebf-6ea20a3a902d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e80dcef6-8cf3-58d4-8627-98be0f13b772" "answer-6ebb2cb7-894c-5ea1-8fe9-5d932e0eaec2" "answer-bc944f96-6c8b-5c8c-9ec9-40c54f081a5b" "answer-ead5149a-8ad0-50cd-aebf-6ea20a3a902d" "answer-c290b836-3e40-5e91-84ff-1cbd84d8ae28"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e80dce